.TP
\f[B]ELEBAKE_PAGER\f[R]
The pager \f[CR]last \(rs<n\(rs> \(rs| sh\f[R] opens on a trace (stdin
from /dev/tty, so it works under \f[CR]... \(rs| sh\f[R]).
No fallback to the login environment: an unset pin is a refusal
.TP
\f[B]ELEBAKE_STATE_DB\f[R]
The state directory of the generated earlboot/elvbootd scripts on the
target (ELV_STATE in the scripts: appraisal, book, heartbeat, spool,
marks, smart counters); created 0700 root by the install steps
.SH FILES
.TP
\f[CR]\(ti/.elebake/db\f[R]
the active database (symlink)
.TP
\f[CR]\(ti/.elebake/<name>/.env/{local,default}/\f[R]
the layered variable store: overrides (\f[CR]setenv\f[R]) over the
installed profile over the shipped templates
.TP
\f[CR]\(ti/.elebake/<name>/.log/YYYY\-MM\-DD/\f[R]
per\-invocation traces \(en the debugging ground truth
(\f[CR]elebake last\f[R])
.TP
\f[CR]\(ti/.elebake/<name>/stage/<stage>/\f[R]
a stage record: \f[CR]boot/\f[R] (the built tree),
\f[CR]backup/<medium>/<label>/\f[R] (backup records), \f[CR]media/\f[R],
\f[CR]marker/\f[R]
.TP
\f[CR]\(ti/.elebake/<name>/provenance/\f[R]
receipts of every admitted import (the lineage)
.TP
\f[CR]\(ti/.elebake/worktree/\f[R]
git worktrees of the FreeBSD source; build trees live outside the
database
.TP
\f[CR]\(ti/.elebake/bundle/\f[R], \f[CR]\(ti/.elebake/incoming/\f[R]
where an exported bundle is handed to the user, and import\(cqs scratch
area
.SH EXAMPLES
Create a database, connect the sources, register keys, build and publish
a stage (every command that changes the database acts by itself; the
pins decide what runs as root):
.IP
.EX
elebake bootstrap current minimal
elebake setenv ELEBAKE_FREEBSD_SRC \(ti/git/freebsd\-src
elebake pkcs11 add db \(aqpkcs11:token=...;object=db\(aq /root/sb/db.crt
elebake openpgp add manifest 4E1F0A2B7C9D8E6F5A4B3C2D1E0F9A8B7C6D5E4F /root/sb/.gnupg
elebake stage add smoke1
elebake stage sign key smoke1 pkcs11 db
elebake stage attest key smoke1 openpgp manifest
elebake stage checkout smoke1 elvboot\-15.1\(ha0
elebake stage make smoke1
elebake stage push smoke1 b
.EE
.PP
Take the database elsewhere \(en one signed pair, pinned on arrival:
.IP
.EX
elebake setenv ELEBAKE_ARCHIVE_ATTEST_KEY manifest
elebake export full \(ti/git/config/dump.sh \(ti/.elebake/bundle/a1b2c3d.tar.gz
# on the receiving machine
elebake openpgp add manifest 4E1F0A2B7C9D8E6F5A4B3C2D1E0F9A8B7C6D5E4F
elebake setenv ELEBAKE_ARCHIVE_ATTEST_KEY manifest
elebake import \(ti/git/config/dump.sh \(ti/.elebake/bundle/a1b2c3d.tar.gz
elebake provenance list
.EE
.PP
The rescue pair, and a rollback that keeps the evidence:
.IP
.EX
elebake export minimized \(ti/rescue/dump.sh \(ti/rescue/bundle.tar.gz
elebake stage backup list smoke1 a
elebake stage rollback smoke1 a known\-good\-p2
.EE
.PP
Inspect instead of act (any command): pin its act terminal to
\f[CR]cat\f[R] (\f[CR]elebake setintp stage_deploy_write cat\f[R]), read
the emitted shell, then pin it back.
\f[CR]elebake\f[R] is the wrapper \f[CR]make install\f[R] places in
\f[CR]$PREFIX/bin\f[R]; from a checkout the same commands read
\f[CR]./elebake.sh ...\f[R].
.PP
A trigger whose when is a composition, and one that runs two actions:
.IP
.EX
elebake trigger add report\-measured \(aqand(when_fail,not(when_skipped))\(aq report_act
elebake trigger add silence\-tainted when_tainted \(aqcompose(taint_act,silence_act)\(aq
elebake trigger show report\-measured
# report\-measured: FIRE(AND(when_fail, NOT(when_skipped)), report_act)
.EE
.PP
A value the loader itself is part of \(en the PCR bank, the loaded
images \(en is expected from the conf, not the binary; learned after a
trusted boot, carried by loaderconf mk, include, sign, push, no build:
.IP
.EX
elebake expectation add pcr\-expected key PcrBank pcr.expected
elebake claim add pcr measure_pcr \- pcr.sha256 pcr\-expected
elebake stage require daily\-v1
# loader.trust.kernellock.pcr.expected  (claim pcr)  MISSING \-\- stage kenv learn ...
elebake stage kenv learn daily\-v1 loader.trust.kernellock.pcr.expected loader.trust.kernellock.pcr.sha256
.EE
.PP
The platform sets, add semantics: import what elvbootd filed per boot,
see what moves, take in what holds, render, build, learn:
.IP
.EX
elebake stage inventory import daily\-v1
elebake stage inventory show daily\-v1 efivars
elebake stage inventory add daily\-v1 efivars 8be4df61/BootOrder
elebake stage inventory add daily\-v1 acpi FACP/\-
elebake stage inventory list daily\-v1 acpi
elebake stage site mk daily\-v1
.EE
